<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{title}}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header" id="top">
      <p class="brand">{{name}}</p>
      <nav aria-label="Site sections">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#sec-1">{{sections.0}}</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sec-2">{{sections.1}}</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sec-3">{{sections.2}}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <h1>{{name}}</h1>
      <p>{{who}}</p>
      <p><a class="button" href="#inquiry">{{mainAction.label}}</a></p>

      <section id="sec-1">
        <h2>{{sections.0}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-2">
        <h2>{{sections.1}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-3">
        <h2>{{sections.2}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="offer">
        <h2>What we offer</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          {{#each items}}<article class="card">
            <h3>{{title}}</h3>
            <p>{{text}}</p>
            <p class="price">{{price}}</p>
          </article>
          {{/each}}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="inquiry">
        <h2>{{mainAction.label}}</h2>
        <form action="/inquiry" method="post">
          <p>
            <label for="f-name">What should we call you?</label><br>
            <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
          </p>
          <p>
            <label for="f-phone">Phone</label><br>
            <input id="f-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required>
          </p>
          <p><button type="submit">{{mainAction.label}}</button></p>
        </form>
      </section>
    </main>


    <section data-scaffold id="request-path">
      <h2>The path of a request to a section’s page</h2>
      <ol id="steps">
        <li class="step">The browser asks for the address of the section “{{sections.0}}”. The web server (nginx) accepts the request and, by a location rule, passes it to the handler.</li>
        <li class="step">The handler (PHP-FPM or an application) receives the request, finds the right section by the address and runs the code.</li>
        <li class="step">The code asks the database for the text of the section and the list of offers.</li>
        <li class="step">The code builds HTML from the data, and the server sends the visitor a response with the code 200.</li>
      </ol>
      <p id="model">Model: a “process per request” and a “living application” differ in that in the first the code starts afresh for every request, and in the second the program lives all the time. For this project I chose the first: it is simpler and suits cheap hosting.</p>
      <p id="cache-place">Cache: the ready page of a section is kept on the disk or in memory for a few minutes. It stores the built HTML, so the code and the database don’t run on every visit.</p>
      <p id="php-hosting">PHP hosting: it suits a project of this kind because it is cheap, and any provider can install WordPress, which runs on PHP. The downside is that PHP is poor at keeping permanent connections, as a chat needs.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>{{name}}, {{city}}</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
`,
