				answer: 0,
				why: [
					'Yes. It is the most important property of the “one request, one process” model: no shared state between requests, and so little chance of memory leaks and odd bugs. The price is having to keep everything you need outside.',
					'No: that is how application servers behave, and they are the ones that get memory leaks.',
					'No: that never happens, and a good thing too, or visitors would see each other.'
				]
			}
